with the release of XCOM to Firaxis  games is bringing numerous changes to  its turn-based strategy formula in ways  both big and small  one of the major additions is the new  Sai operative class a soldier archetype  that uses the aliens mind-control powers  against them so because of the class's  inherent power we've compiled a quick  list of the necessary research options  base facilities and training methods to  add the devastating Sai operative to  your XCOM roster first step kill a  sectoid you'll see these aliens early on  in the game and they'll often  mind-control your soldiers by killing  one of these aliens you'll unlock step 2  which is perform an autopsy on a sec toy  corpse this can easily be done in the  science lab at your Avenger Base and  should only take a few turns step 3 is  to research psionics in the research lab  much like the previous step this can be  done in the research lab and shouldn't  take more than a few days of in-game  time step 4 is to build a Sai lab  facility in one of the open spaces in  your base by adding an engineer to the  building slot you should be able to  expedite the process as you fight more  battles once you have the scilab  facility completed you can move on to  step 5 which is to select a recruit to  teach the scythe unlike the normal  soldiers the Sai operative learns their  abilities through studying so as long as  they don't get injured in battle you can  keep teaching them while also fighting  in individual firefights the last step  which is mainly to help the process  along is to station and engineer in the  Scilab to increase the recruits training  speed it's also important to note that  the Sai operative learns new skills at  random so your soldier might begin with  the inspire ability available but have  to learn aura soul fire and fuse and  subsequent turns so there you have it  the Sai operative is one of the many  changes present in the fantastic XCOM -  and especially in late-game missions  should help you overcome the alien  threat  I'll definitely get that
 

